    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2CYyGtgLvq5iRgHjYX2SJe6)_\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Alignment:** nothing is padded with spaces any more. The three spaces before each column are one space stretched (`display (space :align-to N)`) to the column where it starts, so the columns line up in any font, including a proportional one.\n- **Citekeys first, capped at 45:** columns are served by priority (`sp-citations-column-priorities`): citekey and year, then title and authors, then tags. The citekey column takes the width of the longest key but is limited to 45 characters (`sp-citations-column-max-widths`, commit 45221b0). In the `bibliography` repo (master, 15,129 keys) the longest key is 77 characters, then 61, 57, 56; 99% are 44 or less, so only the few longer keys are cut. #410 adds a lint that flags and shortens keys over 45.\n- **Room for titles:** the entry type and `beref` columns are no longer shown (easy to restore in `citar-templates`); tags only get what titles and authors do not need.\n- **Indicators:** emoji 🌿️ link, 📁️ file, 📝️ note, 🎓️ cited (new), with no padding between them. An absent one is a blank of the same width; one stretched space ends the block. The faces and Modus colours from #405 are removed, since emoji have their own colours.\n- **Why an override:** citar builds the padding from the last character of each indicator, so an empty padding would replace the emoji by a space; `sp-citations--indicator-symbols` overrides `citar--make-indicator-symbols`.\n- Docs updated in `docs/tangles/academic/sp-academic.org` (bullet lists); `sp-citations.el` is the matching tangle. No CHANGELOG edit.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Run in batch Emacs with stubs for citar: the width fitting (priorities, tiers, squeezed and wide rooms), the column positions and the indicator block. Not run against real citar or in the GUI; please try `citar-open` with the posframe on.\n- Branch name has no PR number prefix (cannot rename from the cloud session).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9m8fmtgNiBeMPZDGW)_",
